# Summary

The investigation validated authenticity of files  by validating internal file signatures instead of relying on visible file extensions. Using PowerShel, the lab successfully identified a disguised executable through its "MZ" header, demonstrated the risks of extension spoofing, and reinforced the importance of file signature validation during  DFIR investigations.
